title: Council Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
on-arrival: council_policy_timer += 3; month_actions += 1; council_resources = 0 if not council_resources
view-if: soviets_exist and executive_formed
card-image: img/councils.jpg
tags: govt_affairs
#subtitle: The administration of Germany's workers' councils.
#go-to: 

= Council Policy

In Germany there exist parallel state institutions in the form of the workers' councils, or soviets, which currently exist across Germany.

- @kpd_administration: The KPD administration makes its moves.
- @bourgeois_administration: The bourgeois administration makes its moves.
- @spd_administration: We can make moves.
- @independent_administration: The councils do nothing.
- @nothing: We will do nothing.

@kpd_administration
view-if: kpd_soviets
max-choices: 1

With the Communists in control of the councils, they are bound to make use of this.

- @support_kpd_electoral: The councils support the KPD's campaigning efforts.
- @distribute_mutual_aid: The councils distribute mutual aid.
- @kpd_militia: The councils expand the capacity of the RFB.
- @pre_communist_revolution: The councils attempt to seize state power.

@support_kpd_electoral
on-arrival: workers_kpd += 6; workers_spd -= 3 if not spd_included; unemployed_kpd += 3; socialism += 1; rfb_militancy -= 0.01

The KPD has used their position heading the councils to support their own campaigning efforts, championing themselves as the defenders of the workers.

@distribute_mutual_aid
on-arrival: unemployed_kpd += unemployed/2; workers_kpd += unemployed/5; workers_kpd -= welfare; unemployed_kpd -= welfare; rfb_militancy -= 0.03

The KPD has devoted their funds to the councils as a means of distributing mutual aid, acting as parallel welfare programs, which increase their support.

@kpd_militia
on-arrival: rfb_strength += kpd_s; rfb_militancy += 0.01; rfb_militancy += socialism/1000; strife += 1; coup_progress += 2; sa_militancy += 0.05*bourgeois_power; sh_militancy += 0.025*bourgeois_power;

The KPD has used their position in the council to funnel funds and resources towards their militia in the RFB, expanding it as the effective paramilitary wing of the council movement in Germany. The far-right sees this, and begins arming itself, preparing for a confrontation.

@pre_communist_revolution
view-if: councils_initiative
go-to: communist_revolution
frequency: 25

@bourgeois_administration
view-if: bourgeois_soviets
max-choices: 1

With the Bourgeois in control of the councils, they are bound to make use of this.

- @do_nothing: The councils make a point of doing nothing.
- @self_dissolve: The councils self-dissolve.

@do_nothing
on-arrival: socialism -= 1; nothings += 1

The councils do nothing, seeking to leave as much responsibility as possible to the Reichstag. The bourgeoisie hope to render the councils an obsolete and useless force.

@self_dissolve
view-if: nothings >= 3 and not spd_included
on-arrival: councils_exist = 0; socialism -= 4; pro_republic += 2

The councils officially dissolve, under the rule of the bourgeoisie.

@independent_administration
view-if: independent_soviets

You can't fault them, I guess.

@spd_administration
view-if: spd_soviets

With us in control of the councils, we have a variety of options.

Council capacity: [+ council_resources +]

- @expand_reichstag: Expand cooperation with the Reichstag and avoid conflict.
- @integrate_works_councils: Integrate the councils into the existing works councils as purely economic entities.
- @self_dissolve_spd: Dissolve the councils from within, to end dual power.
- @factory_takeovers: Utilize the councils to seize factories.
- @mutual_aid: Use the councils to distribute mutual aid.
- @militia: Utilize the councils to expand the military capacities of the workers.
- @fund_councils: Divert government funds to prop up the councils.
- @donate_councils: Donate SPD resources to the councils.

@expand_reichstag
choose-if: (not left_soviets and not kpd_included) or (spd_r+sapd_r+kpd_r >= 50)
unavailable-subtitle: The current executive of the councils is unwilling to work with a bourgeois Reichstag.
on-arrival: socialism -= 1 if kpd_r+spd_r+sapd_r < 50; reichstag_cooperation += 1; pro_republic += 2; kpd_relation -= 3 if kpd_r+spd_r+sapd_r < 50; left_dissent += 3 if kpd_r+spd_r+sapd_r < 50; bourgeois_power += 0.01 if bourgeois_power < 0.9 and kpd_r+spd_r+sapd_r < 50; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if capital_strike_progress >= 5 and kpd_r+spd_r+sapd_r < 50; ddp_relation += 3 if kpd_r+spd_r+sapd_r < 50; z_relation += 2 if kpd_r+spd_r+sapd_r < 50; dvp_relation += 2 if kpd_r+spd_r+sapd_r < 50

We have expanded the cooperation of the councils with the Reichstag, reducing conflict over political authority, while also sidelining the councils somewhat in the process.

@self_dissolve_spd
view-if: not left_soviets and not kpd_included and reichstag_cooperation >= 3
choose-if: dissolutionist_s >= left_coalition_s
unavailable-subtitle: There is not majority support on the councils.
on-arrival: soviets_exist = 0; socialism -= 3; pro_republic += 3; kpd_relation -= 15; left_dissent += 15; capital_strike_progress -= 1; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if capital_strike_progress >= 5; bourgeois_power += 0.02; ddp_relation += 5; dvp_relation += 5; z_relation += 5

We have dissolved the councils, putting an end to the state of dual power between them and Reichstag, and causing much upheaval and complaint from our leftward flanks, especially from the KPD. Our actions have, however, put the bourgeoisie at ease.

@factory_takeovers
choose-if: not reformist_soviets and not neorevisionist_soviets and not bourgeois_included
unavailable-subtitle: The current executive of the councils is unwilling to engage in such revolutionary activity.
on-arrival: nationalization_progress += 1; bourgeois_power -= 0.1; capital_strike_progress += 6; coup_progress += 5; unemployed -= 3 if unemployed >= 6; unemployed -= 1.5 if works_councils >= 3 and unemployed > 4; works_program += 1; workers_spd += 10*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 10*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 2; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition; coalition_dissent += 1 if capital_strike_progress >= 10; coalition_dissent += 1 if coup_progress >= 8; dvp_relation -= 12; z_relation -= 8; ddp_relation -= 8; workers_nsdap -= 5*(1-dissent); unemployed_nsdap -= 5*(1-dissent); left_strength += 15; reformist_dissent += 10; left_dissent -= 10; new_middle_spd -= 5; new_middle_spd += 2 if new_middle_conscious; old_middle_spd -= 10; factory_takeovers += 1; economy_goal_completed += 1; kpd_relation += 5*(1-dissent); inflation += 3; economic_growth += 1 if economic_growth < 3; socialism += 1
achievement: wirtschaftspolitik

The capitalists are, predictably, up in arms about our policy of  factory occupations. They call it illegal expropriation, and it is. Nevertheless, it is clear that they have failed, and we must take radical action.

Fascists have been taking increasingly violent actions around the occupied factories, calling us thieves and looters. However, the some of the working-class supporters of the fascists have been peeled off, or at least the ones with a sense of class solidarity.

@mutual_aid
subtitle: -1 council resource
choose-if: council_resources >= 1
on-arrival: unemployed_spd += 8*(1-dissent); unemployed_kpd += 3*(1-dissent) if kpd_included; unemployed_sapd += 3*(1-dissent) if sapd_included; unemployed_nsdap -= (socialism/10); workers += council_resources/10; unemployed -= council_resources/10; council_resources -= 1

Using the councils as framework, we distribute mutual aid. This helps alleviate the pains that many unemployed people are finding, and even helps them to find work, greatly bolstering the reputation of socialism amongst these people as an actually practical politick even when detached from traditionally reformist avenues.

@militia
subtitle: -1 council resource
choose-if: council_resources >= 1
on-arrival: rb_militancy += (council_resources/50)*(left_strength/100); rfb_militancy += (council_resources/100); rfb_militancy += (council_resources/100) if kpd_included; reformist_dissent += 5; z_relation -= 5; ddp_relation -= 5; dvp_relation -= 5; coup_progress += 2; council_resources -= 1

Using the councils as framework, we distribute arms amongst the workers, and begin to train them into closer-knit workers' militias.


@nothing
view-if: spd_soviets

See you later, punk.